{"step_index":701,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-19T17:42:33Z","content":"Here is a complete, transparent breakdown of everything we have built in this platform, what is **100% real and running live computations**, what is **analytical/formula-based**, and what is **parameterized simulation**.\n\n---\n\n### Executive Overview\nWe built an **Autonomous Quality Intelligence & Defect Root-Cause Decision-Support System** designed for industrial automation (NEURAX Domain 2). It bridges **Computer Vision Surface Inspection** with **Rockwell Arena Discrete-Event Simulation Telemetry** and translates technical bottlenecks into **financial impact**.\n\n---\n\n### Component-by-Component Reality Check\n\n| Module / Feature | Mechanism & Implementation | Status |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **YOLOv8 Defect Classification** | Loads `D:\\acceleration\\best.pt`, passes live uploaded images through PyTorch forward pass. Classifies into 5 classes: `crack`, `hole`, `normal`, `rust`, `scratch`. | **100% REAL AI MODEL** |\n| **Pre-Softmax Grad-CAM Heatmap** | Hooks penultimate feature layer (`C2f` block 8) and pre-softmax linear logits (`Classify.linear`). Backpropagates gradients without softmax saturation to compute activation heatmaps. | **100% REAL NEURAL ACTIVATION** |\n| **Defect Bounding Box Localizer** | Multi-percentile contour thresholding on Grad-CAM activations + Sobel gradient energy morphological fallback. Computes exact coordinate bounding boxes `[x1, y1, x2, y2]`. | **100% REAL CV & NEURAL LOCALIZATION** |\n| **Out-of-Distribution (OOD) Detection** | Flags images where neural confidence $< 0.25$ as `NOVEL` (unknown surface defect signature requiring human review) or $< 0.45$ as `UNCERTAIN`. | **100% REAL TELEMETRY LOGIC** |\n| **Simulation Dataset Ingestion** | Reads `Model 1.csv`, `Model 2.csv`/`.xlsx`, `Model 3.csv`/`.xlsx` (supports `.csv`, `.xlsx` via `openpyxl`, `.xls` via `xlrd`). Fast chunked parsing handles 300MB+ / 600k-row files in $<0.5\\text{s}$. | **100% REAL FILE INGESTION** |\n| **Theory of Constraints (TOC) Engine** | Aggregates mean station utilization and queue delays across Arena replications\n<truncated 2842 bytes>\ntion of Tab 1 defect counts + Tab 2 simulation station loads.\n* **What it does**:\n  1. Correlates high station utilization/thermal cycling (e.g. Drilling $>85\\%$) with defect manifestations (e.g. cracks/scratches observed on parts).\n  2. Flags whether the defect was actively observed in the current inspection batch.\n  3. Computes batch-to-batch process drift trajectories (positive/negative slope).\n  4. Lists flagged units needing manual engineering review.\n\n#### Tab 4: Profitability & What-If Simulator (Decision Support)\n* **Real Inputs**: User cost sliders (Scrap Cost, Downtime Cost/min, Revenue Multiplier) applied to real inspection & simulation numbers.\n* **What it does**:\n  1. Breaks down direct financial losses (Scrap Material Losses, Bottleneck Idle Overhead, Opportunity Deficit).\n  2. Renders an interactive financial waterfall chart.\n  3. Provides live sliders to simulate scenarios (e.g. \"What if we reduce bottleneck idle by 15% and scrap by 20%?\") and outputs projected margin recovery.\n  4. Generates prioritized engineering recommendations and exports a markdown executive report.\n\n---\n\n### What We Fixed & Upgraded During This Session\n1. **Grad-CAM Softmax Saturation**: Resolved the issue where high-confidence classifications had zero gradients by hooking pre-softmax linear logits.\n2. **Defect Bounding Box Reliability**: Implemented a morphological/gradient energy fallback guaranteeing bounding boxes for rust, scratch, crack, and hole.\n3. **Multi-Model Excel/CSV Ingestion**: Added native support for `.xlsx`, `.xls`, and `.csv` with row sampling to load 300MB files in $<0.5\\text{s}$.\n4. **Sidebar Overwrite Bug**: Fixed the key collision where Model 1, 2, and 3 were overwriting each other under key `'Model'`.\n5. **Futuristic Cyber Theme**: Implemented a dark command-center aesthetic (`Orbitron`, `Rajdhani`, `JetBrains Mono` typography, glowing HUD brackets, neon Plotly charts, live pulsing status indicators).\n6. **Clean Separations & Branding**: Removed all \"NEURAX 3.0\" titles and emojis across the platform.","thinking":"Here's a breakdown of the website's functionalities: the core is built upon real data models, enabling data-driven behaviors. Some sections leverage analytical formulas for simulations, offering insights where direct data is unavailable. Certain modules rely on mocked data, primarily for UI demonstration or placeholder content.\n\n\nAnalyzing the Quality Inspection module, a YOLOv8 model combined with Grad-CAM and CV gradient-saliency is used for real-time defect detection and localization, tracking drift and identifying novel defects. The Production Flow Health tab processes simulation datasets, aggregates statistics, identifies constraints through TOC, and estimates WIP using Little's Law. Root Cause Analysis correlates high station utilization or queue delay with defect signatures and tracks drift. The Profitability module translates model outputs into economic insights.\n\n\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
