{"step_index":741,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-19T18:02:15Z","content":"Yes, these MATLAB scripts are **extremely useful** for the platform.\n\n---\n\n### What These MATLAB Scripts Are\n\nIn industrial engineering and Rockwell Arena simulation, running discrete-event stochastic replications takes time. To enable real-time decision-making, engineers train **Artificial Neural Network (ANN) Surrogate Metamodels** using MATLAB's Neural Network Toolbox:\n\n1. **`Model1ANN.m`, `Model2ANNDrilling.m`, `Model2ANNMilling.m`, `Model2ANNAssembly.m`**:\n   - These are **fully trained feedforward neural networks** with exact weights (`IW`, `LW`), biases (`b1`, `b2`), and `mapminmax` input/output normalization.\n   - They map manufacturing inputs (such as part arrival rate / interarrival time) directly to station performance metrics (station utilization, queue lengths, cycle times) for Drilling, Milling, and Assembly.\n2. **`c1s2ANN.m`, `c2s4ANN.m`, `c3s3ANN.m`, etc.**:\n   - Metamodels for specific **Cell-Station configurations** (`c` = cell/case, `s` = station/scenario), predicting localized bottleneck behavior under various routing scenarios.\n3. **`Model1Script.m`, `Model2Script*.m`**:\n   - The original training and validation harnesses used in MATLAB (`fitnet`, Levenberg-Marquardt `trainlm`).\n\n---\n\n### How We Can Use Them in the App\n\nBecause these `.m` files export the exact mathematical forward pass:\n\n$$\\hat{y} = \\text{mapminmax}^{-1}\\Big(b_2 + LW_{2,1} \\cdot \\tanh(b_1 + IW_{1,1} \\cdot \\text{mapminmax}(x))\\Big)$$\n\nWe can port these weights and equations directly into a **Python Neural Surrogate Module** (`numpy`/`scipy`) with zero MATLAB runtime dependencies:\n\n| Capability | What It Enables |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| **Real-Time Neural Digital Twin** | Interactive \"What-If\" sliders where the user adjusts input parameters (e.g., arrival rates, station runtimes) and the ANN instantly ($<1\\text{ms}$) predicts station utilization and queue risks. |\n| **Simulation vs. Surrogate Validation** | Compares the uploaded Arena CSV/XLSX simulation data against the ANN surrogate predictions, showing accuracy metrics ($R^2$, MSE) and residual distribution plots. |\n| **Automated Bottleneck Forecaster** | Uses the surrogate network to forecast when a station will exceed 85% utilization before running a physical batch. |\n\n---\n\n### Next Steps\n\nWould you like to integrate these ANN surrogate models into the Streamlit platform? We can add a **\"Digital Twin & ANN Surrogate Engine\"** section with interactive prediction sliders and validation curves.","thinking":"These are ANN surrogate metamodels built from discrete-event simulation data. Their function is to provide faster-running approximations of complex simulation models. Initial focus should be understanding how these metamodels accelerate performance, especially in a platform like Streamlit.\n\n\n"}
